		"nodes": {
			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "COUNTER\nThe counter is a node that counts up or down upon a trigger. The node will keep counting until it is reset. A start value can be set to determine where the counter starts. A step value can be set to set the increments of each step. This is a great tool for sequencing movement or simply counting up to a point. Works really well with the Wrap node.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n•  The Metronome generates triggers for the Counter.\n•  Each time triggered, the Counter goes up by 0.1.\n•  The output is sent to the Wrap node which wraps the value when it exceeds it’s max of 0.9.\n•  This value modulates the height of the Rectangle."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 263,
					"width": 712,
					"x": 108.203125,
					"y": 80.9921875
				},
